{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato","suddhaso"],"title":"22. Hell","html":"<section class='range'  id='dhp306-319'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Khuddakanikāya </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Minor Collection </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Collection of Minor Texts </span></li>\n<li class='subdivision'><span class='root'>Dhammapada </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sayings of the Dhamma 306–319 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Verses of Dhamma </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='range-title'><span class='root'>Nirayavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>22. Hell </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>The Hell Chapter </span></h1></header>\n<article id='dhp306'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Sundarīparibbājikāvatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Abhūtavādī nirayaṁ upeti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>A liar goes to hell, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Those who proclaim what never happened go to hell, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yo vāpi katvā na karomi cāha; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>as does one who denies what they did. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>as well as those who do something then say they did not. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ubhopi te pecca samā bhavanti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Both are equal in the hereafter, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>After death, both are the same; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Nihīnakammā manujā parattha. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>those men of base deeds. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>people whose afterlife was determined by lowly actions. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp307'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Duccaritaphalapīḷitavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Kāsāvakaṇṭhā bahavo, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Many who wear a scrap of ocher cloth </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Many who wear ochre on their neck </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>pāpadhammā asaññatā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>are unrestrained and wicked. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>are evil and unrestrained. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Pāpā pāpehi kammehi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Being wicked, they are reborn in hell </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Because of their evil actions </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>nirayaṁ te upapajjare. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>due to their bad deeds. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>they are reborn in hell. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp308'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Vaggumudātīriyabhikkhuvatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Seyyo ayoguḷo bhutto, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>It’d be better for the immoral and unrestrained </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>It is better to eat a red-hot iron ball, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>tatto aggisikhūpamo; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>to eat an iron ball, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>glowing like fire, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yañce bhuñjeyya dussīlo, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>scorching, like a burning flame, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>than for an immoral, unrestrained person </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>raṭṭhapiṇḍamasaññato. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>than to eat the nation’s alms. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>to eat the nation’s almsfood. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp309'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Khemakaseṭṭhiputtavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Cattāri ṭhānāni naro pamatto, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Four things befall a heedless man </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Four things happen to a negligent person </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Āpajjati paradārūpasevī; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>who sleeps with another’s wife: </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>who commits adultery: </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Apuññalābhaṁ na nikāmaseyyaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>wickedness, poor sleep, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>bad karma, insomnia, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Nindaṁ tatīyaṁ nirayaṁ catutthaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>ill-repute, and rebirth in hell. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>criticism, and rebirth in hell. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp310'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Apuññalābho ca gatī ca pāpikā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>He accrues wickedness and is reborn in a bad place, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>One acquires bad karma and the destiny of evil people, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Bhītassa bhītāya ratī ca thokikā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>all so a frightened couple <j>may snatch a moment’s pleasure, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and only the minute pleasure of a frightened man with a frightened woman; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Rājā ca daṇḍaṁ garukaṁ paṇeti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>for which rulers impose a heavy punishment. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and then the king enacts a severe punishment. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tasmā naro paradāraṁ na seve. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>That’s why a man should not <j>sleep with another’s wife. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Therefore, one should not commit adultery. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp311'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Dubbacabhikkhuvatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Kuso yathā duggahito, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>When kusa grass is wrongly grasped </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Just as a blade, when poorly held, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>hatthamevānukantati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>it only cuts the hand. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>cuts the hand that holds it, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Sāmaññaṁ dupparāmaṭṭhaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>So too, the ascetic life, when wrongly taken, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>a contemplative life that is held incorrectly </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>nirayāyupakaḍḍhati. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>drags you to hell. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>draws one closer to hell. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp312'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yaṁ kiñci sithilaṁ kammaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Any lax act, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Lax behavior, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>saṅkiliṭṭhañca yaṁ vataṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>any corrupt observance, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>defiled practice, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Saṅkassaraṁ brahmacariyaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>or suspicious spiritual life, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>a suspicious spiritual life - </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>na taṁ hoti mahapphalaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>is not very fruitful. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>this does not bring great benefit. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp313'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Kayirā ce kayirāthenaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>If one is to do what should be done, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>If one will do what one should do, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>daḷhamenaṁ parakkame; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>one should staunchly strive. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>then one should make a solid effort, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Sithilo hi paribbājo, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>For the life gone forth when laxly led </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>because a lax renunciant </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>bhiyyo ākirate rajaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>just stirs up dust all the more. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>scatters more dust. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp314'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Issāpakataitthivatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Akataṁ dukkaṭaṁ seyyo, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>A bad deed is better left undone, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>It is better when misconduct is not done; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>pacchā tappati dukkaṭaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>for it will plague you later on. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>misconduct torments afterwards. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Katañca sukataṁ seyyo, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>A good deed is better done, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>It is better when good conduct is done; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>yaṁ katvā nānutappati. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>one that does not plague you. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>after doing so, one is not tormented. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp315'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Sambahulabhikkhuvatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Nagaraṁ yathā paccantaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>As a frontier city </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>As a border city </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>guttaṁ santarabāhiraṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>is guarded inside and out, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>is guarded inside and out, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Evaṁ gopetha attānaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>so you should ward yourselves—</span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>in the same way guard yourself; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>khaṇo vo mā upaccagā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>don’t let the moment pass you by. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>let not a moment slip past you. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Khaṇātītā hi socanti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>For if you miss your moment </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>When the moment is past they sorrow, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>nirayamhi samappitā. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>you’ll grieve when sent to hell. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>those who arrived in hell. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp316'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Nigaṇṭhavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Alajjitāye lajjanti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Unashamed of what is shameful, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>They are ashamed when they should not be ashamed, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>lajjitāye na lajjare; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>ashamed of what is not shameful; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>they are not ashamed when they should be ashamed; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Micchādiṭṭhisamādānā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>beings who uphold wrong view </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>taking up wrong view, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sattā gacchanti duggatiṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>go to a bad place. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>beings go to a bad destination. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp317'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Abhaye bhayadassino, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Seeing danger where there is none, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>They see danger where there is no danger, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>bhaye cābhayadassino; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and blind to the actual danger, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>they see no danger where there is danger; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Micchādiṭṭhisamādānā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>beings who uphold wrong view </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>taking up wrong view, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sattā gacchanti duggatiṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>go to a bad place. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>beings go to a bad destination. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp318'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Titthiyasāvakavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Avajje vajjamatino, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Seeing fault where there is none, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>They think the blameless is blameworthy, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>vajje cāvajjadassino; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and blind to the actual fault, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and see the blameworthy as blameless; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Micchādiṭṭhisamādānā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>beings who uphold wrong view </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>taking up wrong view, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sattā gacchanti duggatiṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>go to a bad place. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>beings go to a bad destination. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp319'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Vajjañca vajjato ñatvā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Knowing a fault as a fault </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Knowing the blameworthy as blameworthy </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>avajjañca avajjato; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and the faultless as faultless, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and the blameless as blameless, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Sammādiṭṭhisamādānā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>beings who uphold right view </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>taking up right view, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sattā gacchanti suggatiṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>go to a good place. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>beings go to a good destination. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endvagga'><span class='root'>Nirayavaggo dvāvīsatimo. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></p></article></section>"}
